# Source snapshots are provenance records. `validate_data()` compares their SHA-256
# against source_manifest.csv, and the weekly cron runs that check on a Linux checkout,
# so git must store and return the exact bytes that were fetched. `-text` disables
# end-of-line normalisation for these paths; without it git rewrote CRLF to LF on the way
# in and every CI run failed on a hash mismatch that no local run could reproduce.
#
# Do not narrow this to *.html. The GRID3 boundary snapshot is JSON and is hashed by the
# same manifest, so it needs the same guarantee.
data/delivery/source_snapshots/*.html -text
data/delivery/source_snapshots/*.geojson -text
